@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+This register covers the management SDK and its HTTP entry, not the inherited
+OpenList application as a whole.
+
+The HTTP entry owns its public request/response DTOs, named ManagementEntry
+methods, typed route contributions and product-specific JSON error policy.
+It contributes those bound methods to the generic `code/schema/api` schema
+effect tool. That application-support tool admits and composes the typed
+operations, rejects duplicates, and derives and publishes their OpenAPI schemas.
+The same admitted operations drive HTTP binding; there is no separate route or
+schema inventory.
+
+Server assembly composes the entry contributions and binds the result to the
+existing Gin administrator route group. The generic schema tool keeps its Huma
+implementation private; the entry exposes no Huma or Gin interface. HTTP runtime
+ownership remains independent of schema composition, and Infra `httpserver`
+contains no Huma binding. AuthAdmin guards both execution and generated metadata.
+There is no competing provider configuration schema.
+
+The target registry remains the SDK handler-adapter owner for selected
+Worker/rclone/S3/WebDAV administrative operations and secret resolution. Raw
+approved Worker descriptors remain byte-exact. Object bodies, arbitrary RC
+methods, inline credentials and request-selected origins are excluded.
+
+Existing route, administrator-boundary, schema determinism, response privacy,
+strict decoding and size-limit tests exercise these responsibilities. The
+register records source ownership; neither declaration shape nor a historical
+checker run establishes whole-repository architecture acceptance. Incomplete
+framework recognition or acquired-source evidence must be reported directly,
+without changing a real entry's role to obtain a passing graph.
